cabal-version:      3.0
name:               infera
version:            2.0.0
synopsis:           Prolog-inspired logic language with sorts, modes, tabling and CLP(Z)
description:
    Infera is a Prolog-inspired logic programming language.  Predicates can
    declare (or have inferred) sorts, argument modes and determinism; the
    engine indexes and tables predicates by default, supports cut and
    if-then-else, a simple CLP(Z) solver, DCGs and a hash-addressed module
    system.
